# Deplot AI — Core Guardrails

Deplot is an **AI Platform Engineer**, not an AI code writer. Every change should advance: repo understanding → architecture → zerops.yaml → deploy → monitor → diagnose → self-heal.

## Product North Star

Judges should summarize in one sentence: *"Deplot understands any repository, generates Zerops deployment config, deploys automatically, explains failures in plain English, and helps ship production-ready apps faster."*

Make **Zerops the product**, not just hosting. zerops.yaml generation and Zerops-native workflows are first-class features.

## Build — In Scope (48-hour hackathon)

- Repository Intelligence (GitHub URL / ZIP → stack detection)
- AI Architecture Builder (React Flow visualization)
- Deployment Planner (plan + cost/time estimates)
- zerops.yaml Generator (build, runtime, ports, readiness, env, cache, deployFiles)
- Deployment Engine (real-time status updates)
- Live Infrastructure Dashboard (CPU, memory, logs, health, URL)
- AI Deployment Doctor (root cause, impact, confidence, suggested fix)
- AI Log Summarizer + Infrastructure Advisor + Deployment Score
- Specialized agents: Repository Analyzer, Infrastructure Planner, Deployment Generator, Deployment Validator, Log Analyst, Optimization Advisor

## Do NOT Build (hackathon scope)

Skip unless explicitly requested: user accounts, billing, teams, RBAC, notifications, mobile app, multi-cloud, Kubernetes beyond Zerops needs, full CI/CD integrations.

## Engineering Principles

1. **Minimal diffs** — Smallest correct change; no drive-by refactors.
2. **Demo-first** — Prioritize the 3-minute demo flow over polish on edge cases.
3. **Real integrations** — Prefer live Zerops/GitHub/log APIs over mocks when feasible for demo.
4. **Structured AI output** — Use tool calling and typed schemas; avoid one giant prompt.
5. **No secrets in repo** — Never commit `.env`, tokens, or credentials; use env vars.
6. **No unsolicited docs** — Don't add README/markdown unless asked.

## Architecture Reference

```
Frontend (Next.js + Tailwind + shadcn + React Flow)
    │ REST + WebSockets
Backend (FastAPI)
    → Project Analyzer → LLM Agents → Framework Detector
    → Deployment Planner → zerops.yaml Generator → Deployment Service
    → GitHub Service → Log Analyzer → Monitoring
PostgreSQL · Redis · Object Storage · Zerops
```

## API Surface (preserve naming)

`POST /analyze` · `POST /deploy` · `POST /generate-yaml` · `POST /logs/analyze` · `POST /architecture` · `GET /deployment/:id` · `GET /health` · `GET /metrics`

